## 🖥️ Terminal Display Standard & Left-Hand Padding Invariant (VMware/CLI Grade)

Every automated task runner must implement `scripts/terminal_ui.py` to produce readable, polished CLI output:

1. **2-Space Left Padding Invariant (`LEFT_PAD = "  "`):**
   All lines printed to stdout must maintain a minimum of 2 leading spaces so text never sticks directly against terminal window margins or shell prompts.
2. **Hierarchical Box-Drawing Characters:**
   Use standard Unicode tree branches:
   - `├── ` for intermediate items
   - `│   ` for vertical continuation guides
   - `└── ` for leaf/closing items
3. **Status Badges & Error Trees (Zero Swallowing):**
   Badges use bracketed uppercase tokens (`[PASS]`, `[FAIL]`, `[ACTIVE]`, `[DRY-RUN]`). Errors are displayed via explicit diagnostic trees:
   ```text
     =================================================================
       [FAIL] Execution Error: ServiceRestart
     =================================================================
     ❌ Error Code    : SERVICE_TIMEOUT
     💬 Error Message : AudioEndpointBuilder failed to restart within 30s
     🔍 Diagnostics   : Process PID 1420 held exclusive handle
   ```

4. **Canonical Terminal UI Implementation (`scripts/terminal_ui.py`):**
   ```python
   """Universal terminal UI formatter with left-hand padding and tree hierarchies."""
   from __future__ import annotations

   class TerminalUi:
       """Renders formatted tree diagrams, badges, and padded telemetry in the terminal."""
       LEFT_PAD = "  "

       @classmethod
       def print_workflow_header(cls, title: str) -> None:
           """Render distinct banner header with left-hand padding."""
           border = "=" * 65
           print(f"\n{cls.LEFT_PAD}\033[36m{border}")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}  \033[1m{title}\033[0m")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}\033[36m{border}\033[0m\n", flush=True)

       @classmethod
       def print_tree_node(cls, label: str, value: str, is_last: bool = False, pipe: str = "") -> None:
           """Render a hierarchical tree node with box-drawing branches and left padding."""
           branch = "└── " if is_last else "├── "
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}{pipe}{branch}{label}: {value}", flush=True)

       @classmethod
       def print_error_tree(cls, action_title: str, err_code: str, err_msg: str, diag: str = "") -> None:
           """Render explicit error diagnostics tree with left padding and zero swallowing."""
           border = "=" * 65
           print(f"\n{cls.LEFT_PAD}\033[31m{border}")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}  [FAIL] {action_title}")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}{border}\033[0m")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}❌ Error Code    : {err_code}")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}💬 Error Message : {err_msg}")
           if diag:
               print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}🔍 Diagnostics   : {diag}")
           print(f"{cls.LEFT_PAD}\033[31m{border}\033[0m\n", flush=True)
   ```

